---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../components/CodeBlock.astro";

const buildCommands = `git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/quitepicky/considered.git
cd considered
go build -o bin/considered ./cmd/considered
go build -o bin/considered-scc ./cmd/considered-scc`;

const varianceCommand = `considered variance add \\
  --subject src/parser/grammar.ts \\
  --metric scc.code_lines \\
  --kind architectural \\
  --reason "Grammar definitions are intentionally centralized."`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Quick start"
  description="Install Considered, initialize configuration, and run a check."
  current="/quick-start/"
>
  <article class="doc">
    <h1>Quick start</h1>
    <p>
      Considered ships as two binaries: the main CLI and the bundled
      <code>scc</code> provider. The CLI discovers providers by executable name,
      so both binaries must be on your <code>PATH</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Install on macOS with Homebrew</h2>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={"brew install --cask quitepicky/tap/considered"} />
    <p>The package installs both binaries together.</p>

    <h2>Linux and manual macOS installation</h2>
    <p>
      Download the archive for your operating system and processor from
      <a href="https://github.com/quitepicky/considered/releases/latest">GitHub Releases</a>.
      Releases include Linux and macOS archives for <code>amd64</code> (x86-64)
      and <code>arm64</code>. Compare the archive's SHA-256 hash with the release's
      <code>checksums.txt</code>, extract it, and put both <code>considered</code>
      and <code>considered-scc</code> on your <code>PATH</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Windows</h2>
    <p>
      Download the Windows archive from
      <a href="https://github.com/quitepicky/considered/releases">GitHub Releases</a>,
      extract it, and add the directory containing both executables to your
      <code>PATH</code>. Choose <code>amd64</code> for x64 or <code>arm64</code>
      for Windows on Arm, and verify the archive against <code>checksums.txt</code>.
      The WinGet submission for
      <code>QuitePicky.Considered</code> is
      <a href="https://github.com/microsoft/winget-pkgs/pull/430077">awaiting community review</a>.
      Until it is accepted and indexed, use the release archive.
    </p>

    <h2>Install from source</h2>
    <p>Requires Git and Go 1.26 or newer, with the vendored submodule initialized.</p>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={buildCommands} />

    <p>
      Put both binaries somewhere on your <code>PATH</code>, or add the local
      <code>bin/</code> directory while you are trying it out.
    </p>

    <h2>Initialize a repository</h2>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={"considered init"} />
    <p>
      This writes a starter <code>.considered.yaml</code> to the repository root.
      It fails if one already exists.
    </p>

    <h2>Run a check</h2>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={"considered check"} />
    <p>
      The text report separates failing violations from passing variances and
      near-boundary warnings.
    </p>

    <h2>Add a variance</h2>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={varianceCommand} />

    <p>
      Considered captures the subject's current metric value as the approved
      boundary and writes the variance into the configuration.
    </p>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>
